  "body": "## Change\n\nAdd the AGIECUT Classic 2S wire EDM machine template to the desktop and embedded machine libraries. Mounting the template preserves the selected post.\n\nThe template states the X/Y rapid speed of 900 mm/min, the Z/U/V rapid speed of 600 mm/min and U/V travel of ±70 mm. It lists the four standard wire sizes from 0.20 to 0.33 mm. The X/Y/Z stroke lengths appear in the description. The operator supplies the installed datum, guide planes and cutting conditions. The handbook qualifies its maximum taper angle by guide type and work height.\n\nThe native job post is separate work in #2945. This change does not select an Agie dialect.\n\n## Source\n\n[AGIE, AGIECUT Classic technical handbook, edition 06.2002 C2.1](https://static.gindumac.com/products/9ccc9b7e-b589-49db-9843-eff1da09434c/documents/ES-EDM-AGI-2002-00001.pdf). Section 1.1 on printed page 4 identifies the model group, travels and speeds. Section 5.2 on printed page 44 lists the wire sizes.\n\n## Verification\n\nIndependent checks used head 08601a2bc. All 68 tests in machine, machine_library, mcp_wire_contour and posting passed. Clippy passed on all camcraft-app targets with warnings denied.\n\nThe pinning tests are:\n- agiecut_classic_2s_exposes_the_sourced_axes_and_wire_sizes\n- agiecut_template_refuses_a_wire_job_without_an_installed_condition\n- every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration\n\nThe normal command script selected the exact library name and mounted AGIECUT CLASSIC 2S. An attempted wire job with C110 failed with a missing-condition diagnostic. It created no NC file. Physical travel and cutting were not tested.\n\nThe full quick gate passed 250 of 251 steps in 36.0 minutes. The failing test was a_missing_default_machine_file_refuses_the_post_per_operation. Both the branch and its base safely refused the missing machine with the setup name. The assertion expected an operation name. Neither replay created NC.\n\nThe reached heavy gate passed 198 of 199 steps in 41.8 minutes. The failing pocket3d_hsm bore test measured 3158 moves, 3130 planar moves and 1141 arcs on macOS ARM64. Base commit 20c81cbc1 reproduced the exact same diagnostic. See #2371 for the platform-specific measurement.\n\nThe standalone Generic ISO wire post also reported missing machine codes on a committed contour stream. This template supplies neither a native writer nor an installed condition. The PR remains a draft.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: The machine library includes an AGIECUT Classic 2S wire EDM template with the manufacturer's stated axes, rapid speeds and standard wire sizes.\n\nFixes #2946\n",
